{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39648998",
      "title": "Creating & Using a First Custom Component",
      "sourceHash": "289f274e2ed08b9c374baa673238b6a293150fdd6e1cd43942db773035da5d5b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.09,
          "end": 2.76,
          "en": "Of course when building React apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "you are not limited to this one app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 9.45,
          "en": "Instead, you can and typically will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.45,
          "end": 11.88,
          "en": "build and use your own components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.88,
          "end": 15.75,
          "en": "dozens and hundreds of your own components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.75,
          "end": 19.38,
          "en": "For example, in this basic demo app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.38,
          "end": 22.89,
          "en": "we could put this header related code into a new",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.89,
          "end": 26.82,
          "en": "custom component to make this app component a bit leaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.82,
          "end": 29.25,
          "en": "and of course also to simply learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.25,
          "end": 31.89,
          "en": "how to create custom components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.89,
          "end": 35.52,
          "en": "Now to build such a first custom component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.52,
          "end": 39.21,
          "en": "we can stay in this app JSX file for now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.21,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "though later we'll actually put different components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 44.88,
          "en": "into different files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.88,
          "end": 48.3,
          "en": "But to get started, let's add a new component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.3,
          "end": 50.97,
          "en": "by adding a new JavaScript function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.97,
          "end": 53.549,
          "en": "because as you learned, React components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.549,
          "end": 57.24,
          "en": "are just JavaScript functions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.24,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "So we can add this new function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "above the app function, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 65.88,
          "en": "And since it's just a normal JavaScript function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.88,
          "end": 68.1,
          "en": "we can of course create that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.1,
          "end": 70.23,
          "en": "with the function keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.23,
          "end": 72.53999999999999,
          "en": "and then give it any name of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.53999999999999,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "Just make sure that it starts with an uppercase character.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 80.49,
          "en": "For example, we could pick header as a name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.49,
          "end": 84.27,
          "en": "because my goal here is to take this header markup",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.27,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "and put it into a separate component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 91.41,
          "en": "As a next, and in this case also already final step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 94.05,
          "en": "we should then return a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.05,
          "end": 97.86,
          "en": "inside of this newly created header function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.86,
          "end": 101.8,
          "en": "And the returned value should be the content that should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.8,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "displayed on the screen by this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 110.44,
          "en": "So in this case, this header markup here, this HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 115.83,
          "en": "you can cut this from the app component and paste it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.83,
          "end": 117.60300000000001,
          "en": "into the header component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.5,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "Now, when returning a multi-line JSX code snippet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 126.51,
          "en": "as I have it here, you must wrap it with parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 126.51,
          "end": 128.85,
          "en": "to in the end tell JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.85,
          "end": 131.553,
          "en": "that all this code here belongs together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.54,
          "end": 135.72,
          "en": "Though thankfully when using VS code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 135.72,
          "end": 138.57,
          "en": "you typically don't have to do that manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 138.57,
          "end": 143.57,
          "en": "because if you simply press the format document shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 143.61,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "these parentheses should be added automatically for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "On CodeSandbox, this can also be done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 151.44,
          "en": "by pressing the shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.44,
          "end": 154.68,
          "en": "or executing the format document command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 157.56,
          "en": "or simply if you save the file there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.56,
          "end": 159.57,
          "en": "And with that, we're done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.57,
          "end": 163.383,
          "en": "This is our first custom component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 164.25,
          "end": 167.88,
          "en": "though at this point we have defined it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 170.34,
          "en": "but we're not using it yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.34,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "Now, normally in JavaScript, you would use a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 176.88,
          "en": "by executing it like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.88,
          "end": 180.57,
          "en": "but that's not how you use a React component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 180.57,
          "end": 183.51,
          "en": "Instead, it will be React, the library,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 183.51,
          "end": 186.75,
          "en": "that will under the hood execute these functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.75,
          "end": 190.59,
          "en": "so that it understands what it should show on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 190.59,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "and therefore we're not going to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 195.06,
          "en": "execute this function like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 195.06,
          "end": 200.06,
          "en": "Instead, the great thing about React and this JSX thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.16,
          "end": 203.34,
          "en": "this HTML in JavaScript code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.34,
          "end": 206.50900000000001,
          "en": "is that you can use your component functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.50900000000001,
          "end": 211.50900000000001,
          "en": "like regular HTML elements inside your JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 212.57999999999998,
          "end": 214.86,
          "en": "So if you want to output the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.86,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "of this header component as part of your app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "you can go to that app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 223.77,
          "en": "and use this header component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 228.12,
          "en": "which we defined before, like an HTML element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 228.12,
          "end": 231.54,
          "en": "inside of the apps component JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.54,
          "end": 236.54,
          "en": "For example, here, just make sure you get the naming right",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 236.79,
          "end": 239.46,
          "en": "and your right header with an uppercase H",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 239.46,
          "end": 243.18,
          "en": "because that is how our component function was named.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 243.18,
          "end": 245.7,
          "en": "You can then either write it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 245.7,
          "end": 248.91,
          "en": "with an opening and a closing tag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 248.91,
          "end": 251.16,
          "en": "or you can also take a shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 251.16,
          "end": 254.58,
          "en": "and write a self-closing tag like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 254.58,
          "end": 257.22,
          "en": "Now, what's important to know and keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.22,
          "end": 260.46,
          "en": "about this self-closing syntax though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 260.46,
          "end": 263.79,
          "en": "is that if you are using this syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 263.79,
          "end": 268.79,
          "en": "you always must have this forward slash here at the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.46,
          "end": 273.15,
          "en": "For example, also, when using this image tag",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 273.15,
          "end": 275.67,
          "en": "this built in image element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.67,
          "end": 279.39,
          "en": "there you also must have this forward slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 279.39,
          "end": 282.09000000000003,
          "en": "writing it like this would not be allowed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 282.09000000000003,
          "end": 286.83,
          "en": "but thankfully as you can see, you would also get an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.83,
          "end": 290.52,
          "en": "if you would try to write it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 290.52,
          "end": 293.64,
          "en": "So you always need that forward slash",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 293.64,
          "end": 297.42,
          "en": "also for your own custom components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 297.42,
          "end": 300.81,
          "en": "But with that, if you save the app JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 300.81,
          "end": 303.36,
          "en": "and you reload your preview window",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 303.36,
          "end": 305.67,
          "en": "you should see the header again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 305.67,
          "end": 308.61,
          "en": "this image title and subtitle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.61,
          "end": 312.84,
          "en": "which of course isn't an impressive change necessarily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 312.84,
          "end": 316.02,
          "en": "because that's the content we saw before as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 316.02,
          "end": 318.12,
          "en": "But now we're seeing that result",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 318.12,
          "end": 322.08,
          "en": "with our first custom component being used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 322.08,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "And since as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 328.26,
          "en": "you are going to work a lot with components in React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 328.26,
          "end": 331.74,
          "en": "this of course, is a crucial first step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 331.74,
          "end": 335.55,
          "en": "because now you know how you can create your own components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 335.55,
          "end": 338.88,
          "en": "and as you see, it's really not that difficult.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 338.88,
          "end": 341.22,
          "en": "Of course, we're going to add more features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 341.22,
          "end": 344.13,
          "en": "and learn about more related concepts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.13,
          "end": 348.75,
          "en": "but in a nutshell this is how you do build React components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 348.75,
          "end": 350.373,
          "en": "as a React developer.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}